<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3948] TTL manager continues to track evicted entries</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3948</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Cache uses only heap memory and has eviction and expiry policies. During loading data into cache TTL manager consumes heap memory even if entries were evicted because it still track this entries. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s ok in case of offheap memory or/and swap are enabled but doesn&apos;t make sense in case of using only heap memory.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See also &lt;a href=&quot;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39447690/apache-ignite-cache-eviction-still-in-memory&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39447690/apache-ignite-cache-eviction-still-in-memory&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
